        "notes": "One problem (Q1 Crystallography) with printed parts A (A.1–A.8), B (B.1–B.6), C (C.1–C.10), D (D.1–D.3) = 27 sub-tasks, plus the Introduction and the Equipment section. Printed part points sum to 20.0 (5.0 per part); no total and no problem points are printed, so points/totalPoints are null. The problems document is the IdPhO 2020 (archive folder IPhO 2020) official English text; the solutions document is a pho.rs web printout (22/08/2021, 'Pho.rs: Crystallography') whose answer boxes carry the Russian label 'Ответ:' (kept as printed). The solutions printout repeats each question text before its solution; these repetitions are not transcribed again (the question text is in the statement). The solution of A.1 is headed 'Write the formula 1' while the statement says 'formula 4' (kept as printed in each place). Kept as printed: Cyrillic 'и' in '$\\vec{k}_s$ и $\\vec{k}_i$' (introduction); 'It has a module |F|'; 'Lattice vectors ... has an angle' (agreement error, B intro); 'one of the indicated units cell' (D.2); 'Measured intensities for two different maxima gives' (A.5 solution); 'which values corresponds' (D.2 solution); 'Each next pair of elements were obtained' (C.9 solution); 'All axis of symmetry are presented' (C.1 solution); 'its enough' (D.2 solution); 'Transnational symmetry' (C.10 solution, 'Translational' meant; 'Transnational' is a real word so it is not changed); in the C.4 solution the conjugated integral is printed with the same exponent sign as printed. The solutions printout shows '\\textbf{PG6.}' as raw LaTeX (a rendering bug of the web page); it is rendered here as bold **PG6.**. Phase table Fig. 13 (problems p. 10) and the solution tables (n/cos θ/θ/m, the PG symmetry tables, the MR1/MR2 intensity and transparency tables) are images in the PDF and are transcribed as Markdown tables; in the MR1/MR2 transparency tables the source shades cells grey (dark grey for the values taken as transparent, light grey for other highlighted cells) — the shading is not reproduced. Table row/column labels 'k / h' and 'γ / χ' are our header for the printed side labels k, h and γ, χ. The C.8 table entry '+/- *' is printed so.\n[/problems/0/sections/3/figures/1/caption] Figure 8: Reflexes $(h = 2n+1, k = 0)$ are systematically absent. Note: Reflex $(0, 0)$ with relatively high intensity is omitted here for clarity.",
